rationale:
Issue #2699: ESC wiring detection in the Setup Wizard gave up after 6 s, but seven protocols (HW5, Scorpion, OpenYGE, Flyrotor, XDFly, ZTW, OMP) need up to 10 s to scan all four wiring combinations at 2.5 s each. With TRIAL_TIMEOUT = 12 s, the scan runs to completion with sufficient margin for MSP polling jitter.

The harness drives the real src/rfsuite/app/pages/setup_wizard_esctelemetry.lua through its wiring detection lifecycle with simulated clock progression:
  1. at t < 12 s (t = 6 s and t = 10 s) a running trial remains active and is not cancelled early;
  2. at t > 12 s (t = 12.1 s) the trial times out, stopWith(timeout) publishes MSP cancel to restore FC wiring, and the outcome shows timeout;
  3. user cancel and leaving the step trigger early trial termination.

--self-test restores the old 6 s timeout and requires the 10 s active check to go red.
